RESOLUTION LOG — INC-2026-1030-118 (orders-api / kv-orders-prod)
Operator: on-call (chronological, machine-stamped at entry)

22:16:02  Page: orders-api 5xx rate 41% (dashboard: app insights), HTTP 500 on
          all /orders endpoints. Customer impact window opened at 22:16.
22:17:40  kubectl get pods -n orders: all orders-api pods Running 1/1 — probes
          green, so the failure is at request time, not startup.
22:19:15  kubectl logs -n orders deploy/orders-api --tail=200: every request that
          touches a secret logs
          " keyvault.BaseClient#GetSecret.Failure[(...) respond=403 ...]".
22:22:51  Checked Key Vault metrics (kv-orders-prod): requests, latency and
          errors flat — the vault itself is healthy.
22:26:05  Checked access on the vault: role assignment list shows
          'Key Vault Secrets User' for principal 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004
          (id-orders-api-prod), created 2026-08-14 — unchanged.
22:31:12  Hypothesis: workload identity exchange, not vault authz. The pod's
          projected service-account token now requests
          system:serviceaccount:orders:orders-api after the namespace move.
22:41:37  az identity federated-credential list for id-orders-api-prod: the
          only credential is fic-orders-api-default, subject
          "system:serviceaccount:default:orders-api" — still bound to the OLD
          namespace. Token exchange fails: subject mismatch.
22:44:02  Decision: add a federated credential for the orders-namespace
          service account (keep the old one until rollback window closes).
22:58:19  az identity federated-credential create --name fic-orders-api-orders
          --identity-name id-orders-api-prod --issuer <oidc-issuer>
          --subject system:serviceaccount:orders:orders-api
          --audience api://AzureADTokenExchange — Succeeded.
23:01:44  kubectl rollout restart deploy/orders-api -n orders (fresh token
          exchange); pods Ready.
23:03:10  5xx rate back to baseline (0.0%); /orders returning 200. Customer
          impact window closed at 23:03 — 47 minutes total.
23:11:55  Old credential fic-orders-api-default left in place, scheduled for
          removal after the rollback window (48h).
